  "summary": "A thermal oxidizer destroys volatile organic compounds (VOCs) and odours in process exhaust by burning them at high temperature. The contaminated air is preheated in a recuperator by the hot clean gas, then passes the burner and is held in the combustion chamber long enough for complete oxidation to CO₂ and water.",
